WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.790
Tamzin: It's very important that young
people talk about their problems,

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:07.500
even if it's not just not with us
as a mental health service, but with

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:11.490
maybe school as well, like pastoral
support at school or even family.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:14.797
Fran: When someone is very
young they are still developing.

00:00:14.874 --> 00:00:18.474
So identifying exactly what's going on
for them can be a little bit difficult

00:00:18.474 --> 00:00:22.744
and it's more about what can you help
them to learn to sort of cope with?

00:00:22.864 --> 00:00:25.984
Tamzin: If they're not talking
about their problems, then you don't

00:00:25.984 --> 00:00:27.544
know what else it's going into.

00:00:27.544 --> 00:00:31.744
So if someone's not sharing it and
talking about it, they could be hiding

00:00:31.744 --> 00:00:34.664
it and they could end up, especially
young people we work with, they

00:00:34.684 --> 00:00:36.124
could end up taking their own life.

00:00:36.354 --> 00:00:40.857
Fran: There'll be a lot of the time
people diagnosing and trying to

00:00:41.992 --> 00:00:44.722
label kids with certain disorders.

00:00:44.722 --> 00:00:47.572
When a lot of the time I think it
was just childhood development.

00:00:47.682 --> 00:00:49.822
Tamzin: So we've got - we've worked
with young people who - well,

00:00:49.822 --> 00:00:51.792
I - in the past have worked with
young people in the care system.

00:00:52.612 --> 00:00:56.092
So they're young people that have been
in care for maybe quite a lot of their

00:00:56.092 --> 00:00:59.962
lives, but they're only kind of finding
out that their identity maybe when

00:00:59.962 --> 00:01:01.792
they're kind of late, leaving school.

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:06.742
So they're young people are kind of better
to come to us for therapy and work when

00:01:06.992 --> 00:01:09.142
they are that age, when they left school.

00:01:09.612 --> 00:01:13.664
Fran: I think anxiety and depression
are very common and there's very

00:01:13.664 --> 00:01:16.384
common -  elements of them are
very common in young people, and

00:01:16.384 --> 00:01:17.624
then very common in old people.

00:01:18.074 --> 00:01:21.164
So I think that I just try and work
with what I can see there rather than

00:01:21.164 --> 00:01:25.124
saying, "oh, this person doesn't have
anxiety or this person doesn't have

00:01:25.124 --> 00:01:29.144
depression" because I think that, I think
most of them will have elements of it

00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:30.584
and there's ways we can still help them.

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:33.664
Tamzin: They might have this mindset
of, "I don't want to talk about

00:01:33.664 --> 00:01:34.714
it it's just going to go away."

00:01:35.104 --> 00:01:37.944
But I think we want young people
who can talk and share their

00:01:37.944 --> 00:01:42.809
problems because if they don't then
things can escalate and then the

00:01:42.809 --> 00:01:44.549
problems can be a lot, a lot worse.

00:01:44.819 --> 00:01:48.869
And we find that they're in a really bad
state and they might not be able to get

00:01:48.869 --> 00:01:50.879
help because they're in that dire state.

00:01:51.259 --> 00:01:53.419
Fran: You know, I think there's levels
when it gets to a point as well when

00:01:53.419 --> 00:01:57.704
you might notice with a young person
that they, you know, say anxiety with a

00:01:57.704 --> 00:02:01.244
13, 14 year old, it might just be that
they're going into school everyday,

00:02:01.244 --> 00:02:04.754
it's quite anxiety provoking, or you
do notice when it's something worse

00:02:04.754 --> 00:02:06.584
than that and it's quite chronic.

00:02:06.644 --> 00:02:10.392
And I think at that point you can
differentiate just in terms of if

00:02:10.392 --> 00:02:14.607
it's affecting every area of their
life and preventing them from doing

00:02:14.607 --> 00:02:15.567
things that they'd like to do.

00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:18.327
Then I would say that's when it's
moving towards being more chronic.

00:02:18.917 --> 00:02:22.487
Tamzin: So if they're like troubled and
they've got things going on, it's better

00:02:22.487 --> 00:02:27.617
to share and talk about it because if,
we find, you know, the more we get in

00:02:27.617 --> 00:02:30.767
people that are engaging with us and the
more they talk to us, the more we can

00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:34.807
help and support them to stop feeling
like that and stop feeling low or stop

00:02:34.817 --> 00:02:36.897
being suicidal or stop self-harming.

